# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale nl
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [06:00, 12:00).
# Sources: Algemeen Nederlands Woordenboek, Instituut voor de Nederlandse
# Taal (https://anw.ivdnt.org/article/ochtend).
# "vanochtend" is a single-word today+ochtend surface, the Dutch shape of
# English "tonight", and the ANW carries it as its own entry.
# "vanmorgen" is a synonym of "vanochtend" the ANW also carries as its own
# entry -- here "morgen" is the older word for the morning ITSELF (as in
# "goedemorgen"), not the "morgen"=tomorrow relative-day word it is
# everywhere else in this locale; the two never compete because "vanmorgen"
# is a single fused token, not a split "van" + "morgen".
ochtend
vanochtend
vanmorgen
